Subject: [PATCH] Initialize descriptor storage before copying pass properties

The NPU50XX IDU pass copies a descriptor backed by LLVM SmallVector. With
GCC 16.2.1 at -O2, the inlined copy constructor leaves an infeasible inline
storage path in the object-size analysis: the subsequent write to payload
byte 91 is diagnosed relative to the 64-byte descriptor object. The actual
DpuInvariantRegister payload is 352 bytes.

Default construction allocates the schema-sized payload before assignment.
Copy assignment then copies the same property bytes into that storage.
This keeps the descriptor layout and field encoding unchanged and preserves
all warning/error flags. Only the affected pass's local copy is changed.

Regression: check-descriptor-copy.py compiles the actual affected translation
unit with Ninja's generated command and runs descriptor-copy-probe.cpp. The
unpatched translation unit fails with -Werror=stringop-overflow. The runtime
probe checks 16 literal field encodings, payload size, unchanged neighboring
bytes, and independence from the source descriptor.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU50XX/dialect/NPUReg50XX/passes/setup_idu_cmx_mux_mode.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU50XX/dialect/NPUReg50XX/passes/setup_idu_cmx_mux_mode.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,10 @@
     auto dataSectionOps = elfMain.getOps<ELF::DataSectionOp>();
     for (auto dataSectionOp : dataSectionOps) {
         dataSectionOp.walk([&](NPUReg50XX::DPUInvariantOp invariantOp) {
-            auto invariantDescriptorRegMap = invariantOp.getProperties().getDescriptor();
+            // Allocate the schema-sized payload before copying, so GCC does not
+            // analyze the field write against SmallVector's inline storage.
+            auto invariantDescriptorRegMap = NPUReg50XX::Descriptors::DpuInvariantRegister{};
+            invariantDescriptorRegMap = invariantOp.getProperties().getDescriptor();
             invariantDescriptorRegMap.write<vpux::NPUReg50XX::Fields::idu_cmx_mux_mode>(_iduCmxMuxMode);
             invariantOp.getProperties().setDescriptor(std::move(invariantDescriptorRegMap));
         });
